### Cover the actual Mouse Jump and Cursor Wrap paths

**Severity:** `medium`

The current Mouse Jump fixture uses a nested `MouseJump/MouseJump.Common` path that is not how these projects are laid out, so it does not catch the fallback-label bug. Updating the fixture to the real sibling path and adding Cursor Wrap coverage makes the regression test fail for both edge cases fixed in the map.

```suggestion
test('path product labels use longest prefixes and suppress Settings side effects', () => {
  assert.deepEqual(
    deriveProductLabelsFromPaths([
      'src/modules/MouseUtils/MouseJump.Common/Helpers.cs',
      'src/settings-ui/Settings.UI/SettingsXAML/Views/MouseJumpPage.xaml',
    ]),
    ['Product-Mouse Jump'],
  );
  assert.deepEqual(
    deriveProductLabelsFromPaths(['src/modules/MouseUtils/CursorWrap/CursorWrap.vcxproj']),
    ['Product-Cursor Wrap'],
  );
  assert.deepEqual(
    deriveProductLabelsFromPaths(['src/modules/cmdpal/src/App/App.xaml']),
    ['Product-Command Palette'],
```

